  },
  "sw_optical_depth": {
   "description": "The cumulative optical depth of the water column at interface i, tau(n,i) = sum_{j<i} opacity(n,j)*h(j) with tau(n,1) = 0 at the surface, for each penetrating band n (MOM_opacity.F90: the per-layer optical depth opt_depth = h*opacity of absorbRemainingSW :748-750 and sumSWoverBands :980-982, accumulated down the column). This is the discrete, measure-weighted Riemann-sum form of the Beer-Lambert optical-depth integral tau(z) = int_0^z opacity dz' (esm-spec 4.3.1: a cumulative integral is spelled by multiplying the per-cell measure into the faq body; the integral op is not used because it is a unit-measure mean over an axis, spec 4.2). The consuming component applies the template once per thickness field it needs: the h passed to absorbRemainingSW for the heating path and the pre-flux h of the sumSWoverBands/KPP buoyancy-flux path (MOM_forcing_type.F90:1102, thickness_to_dz) for the netPen path; the index-set names band/iface/layer are bound at the application site.",
   "params": [
    "opacity",
    "h"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "faq",
    "output_idx": [
     "b",
     "i"
    ],
    "ranges": {
     "b": {
      "from": "band"
     },
     "i": {
      "from": "iface"
     },
     "j": {
      "from": "layer"
     }
    },
    "filter": {
     "op": "<",
     "args": [
      "j",
      "i"
     ]
    },
    "expr": {
     "op": "*",
     "args": [
      {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "opacity",
        "b",
        "j"
       ]
      },
      {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "h",
        "j"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    "args": [
     "opacity",
     "h"
    ]
   }
  }
 }
